      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After WWII, connectivity spurred Surf City's tourism boom in the 1950s and 1970s, with vacation homes and fishing piers proliferating.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Surf_City,_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A $54 million fixed‑span bridge opened in December 2018, 1,200 m long and 65 ft high, replacing the old swing bridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.surfcitync.gov/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The bridge’s 50‑foot width allows for three lanes during hurricane evacuations, a unique feature for the town.",
